<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="ChinatownMyChinatown-Bb-Theme" spTempo="205">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1906 (first published 1910)
Composer:	Jean Schwartz
Lyricist:	William Jerome
Form:	32-bar chorus, preceded by a verse
Style:	Tin Pan Alley popular song; early
	 jazz/foxtrot
Key:	Bb but varies by edition and
	performance

The song was written in 1906 and interpolated into the
revue Up and Down Broadway in 1910, when it was
published. It became a national hit in 1915 and was later
taken up by jazz performers; the original sheet music’s
key could not be verified from the available source
excerpts.</spComments>
